WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.530
I want you all to meet Michael Gardner

2
00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:05.400
and his 10-year-old daughter, Ava.

3
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.340
A few years ago, Michael began his journey

4
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.700
to become a seamster and he thrifted old clothes

5
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:15.180
to make new outfits for Ava as a way to bond with her

6
00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.260
and inspire confidence.

7
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:19.610
Oh, Michael, you're like literally the dad

8
00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:21.470
we all wish we had.

9
00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:23.240
Michael taught Ava how to sew

10
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.090
when she was just five years old

11
00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:27.750
and they've been collaborating ever since.

12
00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.512
You have to watch this.

13
00:00:29.512 --> 00:00:33.010
(children cheering)

14
00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:34.260
Hey, guys. Michael here.

15
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.250
And Ava.

16
00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:38.050
Today, we are at Liberty Ministries thrift store

17
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:41.760
hoping to pick up some really cool, unique, fun pieces

18
00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:45.490
that we're going to mix and match, refashion,

19
00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:48.850
and hopefully come up with something really cool and fun.

20
00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:50.714
Wish us luck, guys. Let's go.

21
00:00:50.714 --> 00:00:53.297
(upbeat music)

22
00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:59.040
We are so excited to create new looks

23
00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.290
from the thrifted pieces that we found.

24
00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:04.540 line:15%
I was lucky enough to find a pair of Levi jeans for myself.

25
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:07.290 line:15%
And I found this really amazing blanket.

26
00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:08.780 line:15%
I got a little sentimental.

27
00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:10.112 line:15%
I'm thinking of my grandmother

28
00:01:10.112 --> 00:01:12.787 line:15%
And for me, I have this cute denim shirt

29
00:01:12.787 --> 00:01:17.490 line:15%
which we will upcycle and put new cool details into it.

30
00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:20.790
And I have pink curtains which I will upcycle

31
00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:21.960
and make a new skirt.

32
00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.410
All right, so we're gonna get started

33
00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:25.190
sewing these pieces up and putting together

34
00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:27.720
a cool daddy-daughter look for you, guys.

35
00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.570
I am so proud of my dad.

36
00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:32.440
He has all of these cool and unique ideas.

37
00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:35.480
We can't wait for you guys to see what we created.

38
00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:36.753
Hope you like it.

39
00:01:36.753 --> 00:01:39.585
(audience clapping)

40
00:01:39.585 --> 00:01:41.590
I love them.

41
00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:44.678
Please welcome, Michael and Ava Gardner.

42
00:01:44.678 --> 00:01:47.694
(audience clapping and cheering)

43
00:01:47.694 --> 00:01:50.277
(upbeat music)

44
00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:59.030
Okay.
Give me a high five.

45
00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:01.830
You did an amazing job with that sweater.

46
00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:02.663
Thank you.

47
00:02:02.663 --> 00:02:05.012
I mean, you are really good at sewing.

48
00:02:05.012 --> 00:02:06.095
Thank you.

49
00:02:06.095 --> 00:02:08.698
(audience clapping)

50
00:02:08.698 --> 00:02:11.415
And Ava, I'm so happy to meet you.

51
00:02:11.415 --> 00:02:12.980
Nice to meet you too.

52
00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.030
Oh my goodness.

53
00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:17.440
I have to just tell you I really admire you guys.

54
00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.150
And why did you start doing this?

55
00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:22.780
What was the idea and inspiration?

56
00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:26.717
So, I always say God turned my pain into power.

57
00:02:26.717 --> 00:02:28.170
I grew up without my father.

58
00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.510 line:15%
So, when I became a dad, I wanted to make sure

59
00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:33.800 line:15%
that she had all the things that I longed for

60
00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:35.471 line:15%
when I was a kid.

61
00:02:35.471 --> 00:02:38.760 line:15%
So, it just became the tool that I used to bond with her

62
00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.775
and teach her about love, self confidence.

63
00:02:40.775 --> 00:02:44.120
Much of what I struggle with growing up without my father.

64
00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:46.157
I mean, she's literally my best friend.

65
00:02:46.157 --> 00:02:47.570
Awww.

66
00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:48.563
You know, she...

67
00:02:48.563 --> 00:02:51.563
(audience clapping)

68
00:02:52.666 --> 00:02:54.600
How do you feel about having a dad

69
00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.410
who says something like that?

70
00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:58.610
I love my dad and I really feel like

71
00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:01.330 line:15%
he understands how much I love him.

72
00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:04.793 line:15%
So, for him to say that makes me feel so good.

73
00:03:04.793 --> 00:03:06.843
(laughs)

74
00:03:06.843 --> 00:03:09.528
(audience clapping)

75
00:03:09.528 --> 00:03:11.553
And you deserve that.

76
00:03:11.553 --> 00:03:15.670
But why sewing? What gave you the idea for sewing?

77
00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:18.880
So, what's interesting is my grandma actually sewed

78
00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.560
for my mom and my aunts

79
00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:23.550
when she was (clears throat) raising them.

80
00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:26.570
My sister actually grabbed my mom's sewing machine

81
00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:29.890 line:15%
and started sewing and I just saw it and just was inspired.

82
00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:33.310 line:15%
And then, kind of watching Ava's personality.

83
00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:35.680 line:15%
She's kinda sassy and fun.

84
00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:37.860
So, I just felt like maybe she would enjoy modeling.

85
00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.840
So, I grabbed the machine, went thrifting,

86
00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:41.970
started making her clothes

87
00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:45.099
and I just put the phone up to her and she started posing

88
00:03:45.099 --> 00:03:48.430
and here we are seven years later.

89
00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:52.440
And Ava, what is this like for you?

90
00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:54.290
You've got this awesome dad.

91
00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:56.650
And he has this really fun idea

92
00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:59.110
that's really unique and interesting.

93
00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:00.380
What did you think?

94
00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:02.030
Were you like, "I wanna be a model.

95
00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:03.790
I wanna make clothes too."

96
00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:06.620
Like, what's your side of the story?

97
00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:08.030
I really love modeling.

98
00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:10.690
I feel like it's a big part of me

99
00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:15.260
and I never thought about doing it,

100
00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:17.690
but when my dad started making clothes for me,

101
00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:21.790
I just started to feel confident

102
00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:24.923
and to feel loved and to feel inspired to model.

103
00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:29.199
(audience clapping)

104
00:04:32.146 --> 00:04:35.979
Well, we all love how connected you both are

105
00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:39.350
and the amazing clothes that you create together.

106
00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:44.144
So, when Drew Crew member and founder of Harlem Fashion Row,

107
00:04:44.144 --> 00:04:47.280
Brandice Daniel heard your story, she had a message for you.

108
00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:49.490
Watch this. She's amazing.

109
00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:51.202
Hi, Michael and Ava.

110
00:04:51.202 --> 00:04:53.730 line:15%
I love what you two are doing so much

111
00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:56.680 line:15%
and wanna help you continue to succeed.

112
00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:59.640 line:15%
I wanna personally mentor you both as well as invite you

113
00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:02.950
to our next Harlem's Fashion Row's Fashion Summit.

114
00:05:02.950 --> 00:05:06.290
There you'll be able to chat with fellow emerging designers

115
00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:09.910
and hear from some of the biggest names in fashion.

116
00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:13.380
I'd also love to promote you two on our Instagram page.

117
00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:15.370
You are both so inspiring

118
00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:18.438
and I cannot wait to work with you more.

119
00:05:18.438 --> 00:05:21.170
Wow.
(audience applauding)

120
00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:22.003
(speaker drowned out by clapping)

121
00:05:22.003 --> 00:05:22.836
It was.

122
00:05:22.836 --> 00:05:24.250
(laughs)

123
00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:25.901
Brandice is amazing.

124
00:05:25.901 --> 00:05:27.980
Wow. Thank you so much.
Wait until you get with her.

125
00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:30.060
She wants to mentor you and introduce you to people.

126
00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:31.411
Wow. Thank you.
Thank you.

127
00:05:31.411 --> 00:05:34.411
(audience clapping)

128
00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:38.750
Well, thank you, Michael and Ava Gardner

129
00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:41.490
for being who you are.

130
00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:42.323
Thank you.

131
00:05:42.323 --> 00:05:45.940
Being the epitome of what good dad program

132
00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:47.780
really wants to be.

133
00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:52.010
And I just really am happy to hang out with you guys today.

134
00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:53.246
Thank you so much.

135
00:05:53.246 --> 00:05:55.829 line:15%
(upbeat music)

